# will_equal_paths — of two things equally near, either is on a will's way
#
# Pugilitas is a will to come to blows (attack). The Test Yard holds two people, the farmer and the
# plowman, and the planner's search commits to whichever it reaches first — the farmer (`inspect will`
# reports the plan's own target). The plowman is exactly as near, so the will must accept him too:
# observing him keeps the focus, and thinking on him proposes the attack. This is the case that used to
# refuse, "not on the way", because only the plan's own target was accepted.
#
# That a will names the person in its sentences, rather than the verb's bare pronoun, is asserted in
# will_refuses.cli.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm pugilitas --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
observe plowman
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect-state will "will pugilitas steps=1"
expect-state will "target=farmer"

# Observing the other man: he is on the way too, so the focus is kept and the reason is the goal here.
click keyword 0
choose 1
choose pugilitas
advance 12 180
# The sentence is "Here I could attack the plowman, which is what I want."; its tail is asserted, since
# the head moves with the prose before it and wraps.
expect which is what I want

# Thinking on him: the attack is proposed, carried out by Pugilitas itself.
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose pugilitas
advance 12 180
expect [Pugilitas
expect-not does nothing for it

quit
